  "events": [],
  "notes": [
    "the app isn't named in the file; no source describes its format, so every unit is decided from the file's own values or kept as written",
    "`AltitudeRelativeBarometer` kept as written, holding no reading: it is 0 on every row, as in a file from a phone without a barometer",
    "`Gx`, `Gy`, `Gz` and `GTotal` kept as written, in a unit two checks don't settle: (1) the quietest second, to 1.15 s, reads 0.999 in the axes' magnitude, where 0.9 to 1.1 reads g at rest; (2) the file has no barometric climb in meters to check the boost against",
    "`Yaw` read in radians, from its range and the magnetic field's direction: (1) its largest reading from 0 is 3.1000, where radians stay within ±π; (2) on 22 rows where the accelerometer reads its rest, its y axis is at least 0.2 from vertical and the yaw at least 0.2 from 0, the yaw differs from the azimuth of the phone's y axis from magnetic north, which the magnetometer's and the accelerometer's directions give, by a median 0.000 read in radians and 1.654 in degrees",
    "`Pitch` read in radians, from its range and gravity's direction: (1) its largest reading from 0 is 1.2000, where radians stay within ±π/2; (2) on 24 rows where the accelerometer reads its rest and the pitch is at least 0.2 from level, |sin pitch| differs from gravity's share along y by a median 0.000 read in radians and 0.911 in degrees",
    "`Roll` read in radians, from its range and gravity's direction: (1) its largest reading from 0 is 1.0993, where radians stay within ±π; (2) on 24 rows where the accelerometer reads its rest, its y axis is at least 0.2 from vertical and the roll at least 0.2 from a half-turn, the roll's angle from the nearest half-turn differs from gravity's about y, atan(|Gx| / |Gz|), by a median 0.000 read in radians and 0.786 in degrees",
    "`GyroX`, `GyroY` and `GyroZ` kept as written, in a unit two checks don't settle: (1) only 4 spans of 5 rows turn by 0.1 to 2.5 rad off the full scale, fewer than 10; (2) no axis stops at a gyroscope's full scale of 125 to 2,000 °/s read in rad/s, on 5 rows or more, 2 of them in a row: largest `GyroX` 1.2913 on 1 row, `GyroY` 5.3672 on 1 row, `GyroZ` 1.2715 on 1 row",
    "`Heading` read in degrees, from its range and its wrap's period: (1) its readings, 10.91 to 350.856, lie within 0 to 360, the largest past the 2π radians reach; (2) 1 step between rows crosses north as a heading in degrees does: by more than 300, and, less 360, turning as the steps on either side do, within a factor of 2",
    "`Latitude` and `Longitude` read in degrees, from the latitude's range and the longitude's: (1) the latitude's largest reading from 0 is 40.1, where radians reach 1.5708 and degrees 90; (2) the longitude's largest reading from 0 is 100.2, where radians reach 3.1416 and degrees 180",
    "`Timestamp` read in milliseconds since 1970 UTC, from the clock and the date: (1) over 23 steps between rows, its step over 1,000 lies at most 0.0000 s from the clock's, `Seconds`; (2) its first reading, read in ms since 1970, falls between 2000 and 2100; kept as the time of day in UTC",
    "`AltitudeMSLGPS` and `AltitudeMSLMaxGPS` kept as written, in a unit no second check settles: the file has no pressure in hPa to compare it with, and a GPS's fixes once a second can't show gravity's pull in the coast, and a pad's height above sea level can't tell meters from feet within the weather's reach",
    "`Record` and `Static` kept as written, as numbers with no unit: by their names flags, states or counts",
    "`GMax` and `AltitudeRelativeMaxBarometer` kept as written, as running extremes: by their names the most or least of another column so far, which the reader doesn't tie to that column's unit",
    "`MagnetometerX`, `MagnetometerY`, `MagnetometerZ`, `HeadingX`, `HeadingY` and `HeadingZ` kept as written: by name a magnetometer's reading, in a unit no source states, and the record has no quantity for a magnetic field",
    "`Revolutions` and `RevApogee` kept as written: by name a count of turns or its clock, which no check in the file ties to the gyroscope",
    "`HorizontalResGPS` and `VerticalResGPS` kept as written: by name the GPS's accuracy, in a unit no source states",
    "`Battery` kept as written: by name the battery's state, in a unit no source states",
    "`AltitudeRelativeSerial` and `AltitudeRelativeMaxSerial` kept as written: by name an external sensor's, in a unit no source states",
    "the primary track is empty: the file's barometric altitude isn't read in meters, so the readings withhold on the log; every column is a channel"
  ]
}
